 "answer": "In current LlamaIndex releases, the parameter is **`context_window`**. It is a field on the LLM's metadata (`LLMMetadata.context_window`), and it sets the model's maximum input size in tokens. LlamaIndex uses it to decide how much text fits in a prompt.\n\nFor a custom LLM, you typically set it by overriding the `metadata` property to return an `LLMMetadata` with the desired `context_window`. The related `num_output` field controls the reserved output size, not the input limit.\n\nI'm less certain of the exact behavior in every version, so check the docs for your installed release if the details matter.",
